                    "fact": {"id": "ohl-sefton-1869", "text": {"en": "A Toronto school songbook of 1869 printed an earlier English version, \"Oh, How Lovely!\", a round for three voices, with \"When to rest the bells are ringing\", closer to the German, where later books have \"When the bells are sweetly ringing\"."}, "source": {"en": "H. F. Sefton, Three-Part Songs (Toronto, 1869), p. 41, read from the scan"}, "url": "https://archive.org/details/threeparts69west00seft"}
